  m_Name: rigging
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: GameTerms.Runtime::GameTerms.GlossaryTermAsset
  data:
    Id: rigging
    Term: Rigging
    Abbreviation: 
    Category: 3
    Difficulty: 1
    ShortDefinition: Building the bone and control structure that deforms a character
      model during animation.
    SimpleExplanation: Creating the skeleton and handles that make a model move.
    WhyItMatters: A clean rig determines how expressive, stable, and reusable animations
      can be.
    Example: Shoulder, spine, and finger controls are added to a hero character mesh.
    CommonMistake: Overcomplicating controls so animators fight the rig instead of
      posing.
    PracticePrompt: Build a simple biped rig with IK legs and test a walk cycle.
    GameUses:
    - Character animation
    - Cinematics
    - Facial performance
    RelatedTermIds:
    - skinning
    - uv-mapping
    - inverse-kinematics
    - retargeting
    Tags:
    - animation
    - characters
    - pipeline
    Synonyms: []
